<title>USA: Alliance Imaging buys back debt, prfrd.</title>
<headline>Alliance Imaging buys back debt, prfrd.</headline>
<dateline>ORANGE, Calif. 1997-01-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Alliance Imaging Inc said on Thursday it has completed the repurchase of its 7.5 percent senior subordinated debentures due 2005 and its series A 6 percent cumulative preferred stock.</p>
<p>The securities retired, which are carried on Alliance's balance sheet at an aggregate of $31.6 million, were repurchased for $16.8 million plus accrued interest and dividends in cash, Alliance Imaging said.</p>
<p>Funds for the repurchase were generated through the closing of a concurrent financing transaction, the company said.</p>
</text>
